>But there is something wrong with color.
>
>When mouse in game window, it's all right. but when mouse going to
>outside of window, root screen's color is badlly changed.
>My display's default visual is PseudoColor. So it must be no
>problem...
>

You are experiencing "color flash".  This happens when you use up all of your hardware
color table in one application.  You move to out of the window and the color table gets
swapped out and replaced to supply the original colors.

You can:
- Use fewer different colors (limit is 256 and openwin reserves some colors)
- Get hardware that supports multiple hardware color tables (GS or GT cards from Sun)
- Live with it

